test:clautolisp:macos — BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-AND-FILENAME-HELPERS fails (2 checks)

== Symptom ==

On the macOS clautolisp test lane, the FiveAM test
BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-AND-FILENAME-HELPERS reports two failed checks:

    Running test BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-AND-FILENAME-HELPERS ff...........
    ...
    Did 1549 checks.  Fail: 2
    BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-AND-FILENAME-HELPERS in AUTOLISP-BUILTINS-CORE-SUITE []:
    BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-AND-FILENAME-HELPERS in AUTOLISP-BUILTINS-CORE-SUITE []:

The two failing `is' forms carry no description string (the `[]'), so the
trace shows only the count. The rest of the test (the "..........") passes.

== Scope / not a regression ==

- macOS ONLY: test:clautolisp:windows and the Linux suite pass the same test.
- Pre-existing: it fails identically across several consecutive pipelines
  (540f232, 2f151e7, fb38d9a, 0a7aa86 — the G2/G3/Phase-4 encoding commits),
  none of which touch vl-directory / vl-filename. The macOS runner is
  intermittent and had not run for a while, so this only surfaced now.
- Unrelated to the encoding work (ENCODING-FILE-ROUNDTRIP and the CLAL-FILE-
  ENCODING-* tests all PASS on the same macОС run).

== Likely cause ==

A macOS-specific path assumption in the vl-directory / vl-filename helper
test — the usual suspects: /var vs /private/var symlink canonicalisation,
TMPDIR with a trailing slash, or a case-insensitive-FS filename compare.
Needs a macOS box to see which two assertions fire (the descriptions are
empty; add labels to the two `is' forms to identify them, or run the test
locally on macOS with fiveam:*verbose* / (fiveam:run! ...)).

== First step ==

Give the two failing `is' forms in
clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/tests/…builtin…(vl-directory/filename)
a description string so the CI trace pinpoints them, then reproduce on macOS.
